6. STEP 0 — the normal-mode BASELINES, each driven, not merely shown
---------------------------------------------------------------------

STANDING-ORDERS §7 and the dispatch's grading rule: *"a feature that was never configured
proves nothing by being absent."* So every restriction secure mode is supposed to impose was
first **turned on and driven in normal mode**. Everything in this section is run 2's own
scaffolding and is removed in §11.

**6a. Telnet turned ON** (`tools/tb cfg`, 09:42:59):

    >>> service telnet ip
    % Warning: Telnet is insecure and deprecated. Please use SSH.
    awplus(config)#

The `% ` line is the documented advisory of `platforms/x960.md` §7F.3, already in
`console.ADVISORY`; `cfg.py` continued and exited 0. Stored exactly as §7F.1 predicts — the
running-config holds `service telnet` **plus** `no service telnet ipv6`, not `service telnet ip`.

